Yes, you can determine if a Slack message has been read or not using the Slack API. When you retrieve a message using its ID, the API will return information about the message, including whether it has been read or not.

The `read` property in the message object indicates whether the message has been read. If the value is `true`, then the message has been read; if it's `false`, then it hasn't been read yet.

Here's an example of how to check if a message has been read using the Slack API:
```javascript
const slack = require('slack');

async function checkMessageRead(messageId) {
  const client = new slack.Client(process.env.SLACK_BOT_TOKEN);

  try {
    const message = await client.messages.get({
      channel: '#general',
      message_ts: messageId,
    });

    console.log(`Message ${message.ts} has been read: ${message.read}`);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(`Error checking message read status: ${error}`);
  }
}

checkMessageRead('1234567890'); // Replace with the actual message ID you want to check
```
In this example, we use the `slack` library to connect to the Slack API and retrieve a message by its ID. We then check the `read` property of the message object to determine whether it has been read or not.

Note that the `read` property may not be immediately available after a message is sent. It may take some time for the Slack API to update the read status. Additionally, the read status may change over time as users view and interact with the message.

