Here's a simple MATLAB code that identifies the tense used in a given sentence:

```matlab
function tense = identify_tense(sentence)
    % Regular expression pattern to match various tenses
    pattern = '(?i)(?:would|could|should|might|ought|can|may|shall|will)|(?<=^|\s+)(?:been|gone|come|going)|(?<!\d)\b(?:do|does|did)\b';

    % Check if the sentence matches any of the tense patterns
    if regexp(sentence, pattern, 'match')
        tense = 'Present Conditional';
    elseif regexp(sentence, '(?i)(?:have|has|had)\b', 'match')
        tense = 'Present Perfect';
    elseif regexp(sentence, '(?i)(?:be|am|is|are|was|were)\b', 'match')
        tense = 'Present Simple';
    elseif regexp(sentence, '(?i)(?:been|gone|come|going)\b', 'match')
        tense = 'Present Continuous';
    else
        tense = 'Other';
    end
end

% Test the function with the given sentence
sentence = 'I would like to have a meeting today';
tense = identify_tense(sentence);
disp(['The tense used in the sentence is: ', tense]);
```

This code defines a regular expression pattern that matches various tenses, including the present conditional tense. It then checks if the given sentence matches any of these patterns and assigns the corresponding tense to the `tense` variable. Finally, it prints the identified tense to the console.

Here's an example of a Generic REST Service Wrapper Class in C# that includes Auth Token Handling:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Net.Http;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
using Newtonsoft.Json;

public class RestServiceWrapper<T>
{
    private readonly string _baseAddress;
    private readonly string _authToken;

    public RestServiceWrapper(string baseAddress, string authToken)
    {
        _baseAddress = baseAddress;
        _authToken = authToken;
    }

    public async Task<T> GetAsync(string endpoint)
    {
        using (var client = new HttpClient())
        {
            client.DefaultRequestHeaders.Authorization = new System.Net.Http.Headers.AuthenticationHeaderValue("Bearer", _authToken);
            var response = await client.GetAsync($"{_baseAddress}{endpoint}");
            response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
            return await response.Content.ReadAsAsync<T>();
        }
    }

    public async Task<T> PostAsync(string endpoint, T data)
    {
        using (var client = new HttpClient())
        {
            client.DefaultRequestHeaders.Authorization = new System.Net.Http.Headers.AuthenticationHeaderValue("Bearer", _authToken);
            var content = new StringContent(JsonConvert.SerializeObject(data), Encoding.UTF8, "application/json");
            var response = await client.PostAsync($"{_baseAddress}{endpoint}", content);
            response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
            return await response.Content.ReadAsAsync<T>();
        }
    }
}
```

